=== PARITY (web source reproduced end-to-end) ===
  - Data (web useTranslation + the props from FleetStatsWidget → useUnits /
    useFleetAnalytics / useVehicles / recent drives+charges): bound through the P1/S8
    seam FleetStatsSource → FleetStatsBarModel. The web leaf is pure-presentational; the
    native source carries its prop snapshot. No HTTP in the view.
  - The five cards reproduce the web order + wiring exactly:
      1 Fleet Size  — fmtNumber(vehicleCount,0); caption "{onlineCount} online"; text-primary.
      2 Distance(30d) — fmtNumber(toDistanceDisplay(total_distance_km),0)+" "+unit; cyan→accent;
                        sparkline = recentDrives.distance_m reversed.
      3 Energy(30d) — fmtNumber(total_energy_kwh,1)+" kWh"; emerald→success;
                        sparkline = recentCharges.total_energy_added_wh reversed.
      4 Efficiency  — fmtNumber(toEfficiencyDisplay(avg_efficiency_wh_km),0)+" "+effUnit;
                        amber→warning; caption "fleet average".
      5 Alerts      — fmtNumber(unreadAlerts,0); red→danger if >0 else emerald→success;
                        caption "unread".
  - Converters ported verbatim (FleetStatsWidget + lib/unitConversion): distance =
    meters/{1000|1609.344|0.3048}; efficiency Wh/km → Wh/mi ×1.609344 on `mi`; the SI
    `total_distance_km` value is fed as SI meters (Phase-42; the legacy `_km` key is the
    R2-style misname). EXECUTED-verified: 1,234,000 m → "1,234 km" / "767 mi";
    158 Wh/km → "158 Wh/km" / "254 Wh/mi"; 312.5 → "312.5 kWh".
  - `MiniChart` gate reproduced: the web `if (data.length < 2) return null` becomes
    `showsSparkline` (≥ 2 points), so a 0/1-point series draws nothing (not a stub box).
  - Composition: web `<GlassPanel>` tile → glass-surface tile (label + TSAnimatedNumber
    + caption|sparkline); web `<StaggerContainer>` / `<StaggerItem>` →
    TSStaggerContainer/TSStaggerItem cascade; web `grid-cols-2 sm:3 md:4 lg:5` →
    FleetStatsLayout.columnCount (640/768/1024 px), unit-tested.
  - Unit symbols ("km" / "kWh" / "Wh/km") are locale-invariant codes appended in the
    pure core verbatim (web passes them as data; same disposition as SummaryStatsRow's
    "%"). Translatable prose (labels + online/average/unread) routes through P1/S10.

